※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=1 diag=none

※ A condition the compiler settles costs nothing: nothing of it reaches the
※ binary, and the report log is where a reader is told so.  This one is a
※ question about types, which is settled and lowered nowhere -- a lift is not a
※ value, so a condition holding one has to be answered before anything tries to
※ lower it.

fn step(a: u8) → u8 pre(⌜u8⌝ ≠ ⌜u16⌝):
    a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(step(1u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
